{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Of the Jashubite.</b> This is the Yob mentioned among those who went down to Egypt, for all the families were named after those who went down to Egypt, and those born from them onward were not named after them as families — except for the families of Ephraim and Manasseh, all of whom were born in Egypt, and Ard and Naaman, sons of Bela son of Benjamin. And I found in the foundation of Rabbi Moshe ha-Darshan that their mother went down from Egypt when she was pregnant with them; therefore they were divided into families — like Hezron and Hamul, who were grandsons of Judah, and Heber and Malkiel, who were grandsons of Asher. And if this is an aggadah, well and good; and if not, I say that Bela had many grandsons, and from these two — Ard and Naaman — there issued from each a great family, and the descendants of the other sons were named after Bela, while the descendants of these two were named after them. And so I say concerning the sons of Machir, who were divided into two families: one named after him, and one named after Gilad his son. Five families were lacking from the sons of Benjamin. Here was fulfilled part of the prophecy of his mother, who called him בֶּן אוֹנִי — 'son of my affliction' — and in the concubine at Giveah (Judges 20) it was fulfilled entirely. This I found in the foundation of R. Moshe ha-Darshan."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:53.903181134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}